---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../config/site';
import { byId } from '../lib/measures';
import { LESSONS } from '../lib/learn';
import { headlineText } from '../lib/format';
// 6 measures mapped to senior Economics and Civics topics.
const SET = [
  ['inflation', 'Inflation and the price level'], ['unemployment', 'The labour market'], ['gdp_per_capita', 'Economic growth and living standards'],
  ['real_wages', 'Wages and real income'], ['interest_rates', 'Monetary policy'], ['gross_debt', 'Fiscal policy and public debt'],
].map(([id, topic]) => ({ m: byId(id)!, topic })).filter((x) => x.m);
---
<Base title="For classrooms: Economics and Civics figures" description="6 official measures mapped to senior Economics and Civics topics, with 20-year charts, downloads, plain-English explainers, a Budget simulator and a referencing guide. Same rules whichever party governs." section="learn/">
  <div class="wrap pt-10 md:pt-14">
    <p class="eyebrow">For classrooms</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-2 text-[clamp(34px,4.6vw,52px)]">Official figures, ready for the classroom</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-3 max-w-[70ch]">Everything on this site is an official figure from the ABS, the Reserve Bank, Treasury or Parliament, with the source linked. The site gives no score of its own and applies the same published rules whichever party is in government, so it can go on a classroom screen. Here is the short way in for teachers and students.</p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[15px]"><a href={url('methodology/')} class="font-bold">How the site works</a> · <a href={url('methodology/#selection')} class="font-bold">How measures are chosen</a> · <a href={url('about/')} class="font-bold">About</a></p>

    <h2 class="h2 mt-12">6 measures, by topic</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink-2">Each opens to the latest figure, a chart you can switch to 20 years, the official source, a plain-English explanation and a ready-made citation.</p>
    <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {SET.map(({ m, topic }) => (
        <a href={url(`measures/${m.id}/`)} class="card card-link card-pad flex flex-col gap-2">
          <p class="eyebrow">{topic}</p>
          <p class="font-display text-[22px] font-semibold leading-tight">{m.title}</p>
          <p class="num font-display text-[30px] font-semibold leading-none">{headlineText(m.headline)}</p>
          <p class="meta">{m.headline.caption}{m.headline.period ? ` · ${m.headline.period}` : ''}</p>
          <p class="mt-auto pt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[14.5px] font-bold text-brand">Open <Icon name="arrow" size={15} /></p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2 class="h2 mt-14">Lesson tools</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <a href={url('budget/build/')} class="card card-link card-pad"><p class="eyebrow">Simulator</p><p class="mt-2 font-display text-[21px] font-semibold leading-tight">Build your own Federal Budget</p><p class="mt-2 text-[14.5px] text-ink-2">Students start from the real Budget, change tax and spending lines, and watch the deficit and debt respond. “Copy link to my budget” gives them a link to hand in.</p></a>
      <a href={url('learn/')} class="card card-link card-pad"><p class="eyebrow">Explainers</p><p class="mt-2 font-display text-[21px] font-semibold leading-tight">{LESSONS.length} short interactive lessons</p><p class="mt-2 text-[14.5px] text-ink-2">{LESSONS.map((l) => l.title).join(', ')}. 2 to 3 minutes each, no jargon.</p></a>
      <a href={url('make-your-own-chart/')} class="card card-link card-pad"><p class="eyebrow">Assignments</p><p class="mt-2 font-display text-[21px] font-semibold leading-tight">Make your own chart</p><p class="mt-2 text-[14.5px] text-ink-2">Download any series as a spreadsheet, redraw it, and credit the source in 1 line. Written for a 16-year-old to follow.</p></a>
    </div>

    <h2 class="h2 mt-14">Referencing</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-[70ch] text-ink-2">Every measure page has a “Cite this” box with Harvard and APA versions. The statistical agency is the author and {SITE.name} is where it was retrieved, which is how a teacher or a marker expects it. For a chart a student has redrawn, the source line at the top of the downloaded file is the credit to paste under it.</p>
    <div class="card card-pad mt-4"><p class="meta">Example, Harvard</p><p class="mono mt-1 text-[13.5px]">Australian Bureau of Statistics (2026). Unemployment: 4.7% (September 2026). Via {SITE.name}, retrieved 17 Oct 2026, https://govscore.com.au/measures/unemployment/</p></div>

    <h2 class="h2 mt-14">Before you put it on the screen</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 max-w-[70ch] text-[15.5px] text-ink-2">
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 text-good"><Icon name="check" size={18} /></span><span>The <a href={url('measures/')}>Measures</a> page and any single measure page are the calmest views for a class: big figures, no verdict wall.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 text-good"><Icon name="check" size={18} /></span><span>Dark mode is in the header (the sun icon) if the room is bright.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 text-good"><Icon name="check" size={18} /></span><span>The Promises page gives verdicts on the government’s own commitments. Use it for a lesson on accountability, with the <a href={url('methodology/')}>rules</a> open beside it so students can test a verdict themselves.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta mt-8">Teachers: if a figure or an explainer would be more useful in another form, say so on the <a href={url('corrections/')}>corrections page</a>. Suggestions are read and answered.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
